Summary of Information Covered in the README
The Problem: Processing raw absolute spatial coordinates leads to severe tracking drift, translation dependency, and statistical instability during training.

The Transition (The Split): The input pipeline shifts away from raw absolute position coordinates. Instead, a temporal split calculates frame-to-frame displacement components.

How It Is Done: By calculating the first derivative of the trajectories, the absolute positions are transformed into clean, translation-invariant velocity vectors.

The Benefit: This provides stationary data with a stable mean, bounding the numbers naturally and forcing the network to learn genuine motion dynamics instead of localized grid positions.

Model Context: The 7-channel input architecture of your TCN model (base_tcn_7in.pth) is perfectly calibrated to align with these transformed velocity components to ensure stable gradient propagation.

